{"name":"Foresight","hex":"#94a8d3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"foresight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The ability, or the due use of one's ability, to foresee or prepare wisely for the future.","The ability to foresee future events in a supernatural or paranormal way, such as psychically."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/foresight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Foresight (psychology)","blocks":[{"text":"Foresight is the ability to predict, or the action of predicting, what will happen or what is needed in the future. Studies suggest that much of human thought is directed towards potential future events. Because of this, the nature and evolution of foresight is an important topic in psychology. Thinking about the future is studied under the label prospection."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foresight_(psychology)","wikidata":"Q2073839"},{"title":"Mental time travel","blocks":[{"text":"In psychology, mental time travel is the capacity to mentally reconstruct personal events from the past as well as to imagine possible scenarios in the future. The term was coined by Thomas Suddendorf and Michael Corballis, building on \nEndel Tulving's work on episodic memory."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_time_travel","wikidata":"Q5113942"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"foresight":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-foresight.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-foresight.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-foresight.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b3/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-foresight.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-foresight.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"General Cargo Ship Leanne Auerbach at